# 🛠️ ROBLOX & AI DEVELOPER COMMAND CHEATSHEET

Welcome! Here is a beginner-friendly reference guide covering essential commands for **AI Assistant**, **Rojo**, **Rokit**, **Git**, and your **Windows Terminal**.

---

## 🤖 1. AI Assistant & Slash Commands

Use these special slash commands directly in your chat prompt window to control the AI assistant:

| Slash Command | What It Does & When to Use It |
| :--- | :--- |
| **`/goal`** | **Long-Running Autonomous Task**: Tells the AI to work continuously and thoroughly on a large goal (e.g. building a full system) without stopping for small questions. |
| **`/grill-me`** | **Interactive Q&A Plan**: Starts an interview session where the AI asks you design questions to align on choices before writing code. |
| **`/schedule`** | **Timer & Reminders**: Schedules a one-time timer or recurring reminder for long build/deploy tasks. |
| **`/learn`** | **Save Custom Rules**: Teaches the AI a specific project rule or coding preference to remember forever. |

### 💡 Pro-Tips for Prompting
* **Mention Specific Files**: Use full relative paths (e.g., *"Update `src/client/Controllers/PlacementController.luau`"*).
* **Reference Specifications**: Use tracking files like `v0.0.1_brainrot_castle_story_spec.md` to keep complex features organized.

