## 🔴 2. Rojo Commands (Roblox Sync Tool)

Rojo syncs code from your computer (`src/`) directly into your open Roblox Studio session live.

| Command | What It Does |
| :--- | :--- |
| `rojo serve` | **Most Important!** Starts the live sync server. Open Roblox Studio -> Plugins -> Rojo -> Connect. |
| `rojo build -o Game.rbxl` | Compiles your local code and `default.project.json` into a single standalone `.rbxl` file. |
| `rojo plugin install` | Installs the Rojo plugin into your Roblox Studio plugins folder automatically. |
| `rojo init` | Initializes a new project with a default `default.project.json` file. |

---

## 🚀 3. Rokit Commands (Developer Toolchain Manager)

Rokit automatically installs and manages CLI tools like Rojo, Selene, or StyLua for your project.

| Command | What It Does |
| :--- | :--- |
| `rokit install` | Downloads & installs all developer tools listed in `rokit.toml`. |
| `rokit update` | Checks for and updates your local development tools to the latest versions. |

