## 💻 5. Terminal Commands (PowerShell / Command Prompt)

Basic commands for navigating folders and managing processes in Windows:

| Command | What It Does | Quick Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `ls` or `dir` | Lists all files and subfolders in your current folder. | `ls` |
| `cd <folder>` | Changes your working directory into a folder. | `cd src/server` |
| `cd ..` | Moves up one parent folder level. | `cd ..` |
| `cls` or `clear` | Clears all text clutter from your terminal screen. | `cls` |
| `Ctrl + C` | Stops/kills a running terminal process (like stopping `rojo serve`). | Press `Ctrl + C` in terminal |
| `Get-Process` | Shows running background processes on Windows. | `Get-Process rojo` |

